\begin{CRITIC}
*   **Data-Hypothesis Mismatch:** The proposal aims to use a Gibbs point process to test "spatial regularity" within halos. However, the data generation process explicitly uses an exponential radial profile for satellites. A Gibbs model (pairwise interaction) is fundamentally ill-suited to capture the *radial* density profile of a Neyman-Scott cluster; it will likely misinterpret the radial concentration as "repulsion" or "attraction," leading to a model-specification error rather than a physical insight.
